@startuml 01h-state-node-lifecycle
!include ../_style.iuml
title Pi-Gen imaging: lifecycle of one cluster node, from image to verified member

[*] --> Built : scripts/build.sh
state "Image built\n(generic, role-less)" as Built
Built --> Flashed : write .img to SD
state "Flashed\n(no ivalice-node.conf)" as Flashed
Flashed --> Personalized : personalize-node.sh
state "Personalized\nbootfs has ivalice-node.conf" as Personalized
Flashed --> Halted : boot without conf
state "Firstboot skipped\n(ConditionPathExists fails,\neth0 unconfigured: only the .template\nexists and NetworkManager is masked)" as Halted

Personalized --> FirstBooted : power on,\nivalice-firstboot.service
state "First-booted" as FirstBooted {
  state "hostname + static IP set" as fb1
  state "role units enabled\n(head: slurmctld, postboot-ansible\nworker: slurmd, cluster key deleted)" as fb2
  state "marker /var/lib/ivalice/firstboot.done\nrole.head | role.worker [, k3s.enabled]" as fb3
  fb1 --> fb2
  fb2 --> fb3
}
FirstBooted --> Running : services start\n(see 01i note on same-boot enablement)
state "Running role services\nmunge + slurmctld (head) / slurmd (worker)\noptional k3s / k3s-agent" as Running
Running --> Converging : head only:\nivalice-postboot-ansible (01j)
state "Converging\nsite.yml 10 -> 20 -> 30 -> 40/50" as Converging
Converging --> Verified : 90-verify: sinfo 5 idle,\nsrun -N5 hostname
state "Verified + converged\nansible-postboot.done written\nby the verify role" as Verified
Converging --> Retrying : quorum timeout or\nplaybook failure
state "Retrying\nRestart=on-failure every 120 s" as Retrying
Retrying --> Converging
Retrying --> Failed : start limit hit (if it ever applies)
state "Failed\nmanual: journalctl, /var/log/ivalice/ansible.log" as Failed
Verified --> [*]

note right of Verified
  Re-personalizing a booted node does nothing:
  firstboot.done blocks a second run. Reflash
  or delete the marker to change identity.
end note
note bottom of Retrying #FFE4E1
  FINDING (likely): the unit puts StartLimitIntervalSec= in [Service].
  systemd only accepts that key in [Unit] (the [Service] spelling is
  StartLimitInterval=), so it is ignored, the 10 s default applies, and
  with RestartSec=120 the burst of 5 is never reached: the service
  retries every 2 min indefinitely. Check: systemd-analyze verify.
end note
@enduml
